          "start": 0
        },
        "quote": "The following words, terms and phrases, when used in this title, shall have the meanings ascribed to them in this section, except where the context clearly indicates a different meaning:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:0#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 1",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 1,
          "component_id": "b90a415a-1ed5-5c40-aaa7-61625213de4a",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 450,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:1",
          "start": 187
        },
        "quote": "“Angle or diagonal parking” means the standing or parking of a motor vehicle on a public street with the long axis of the vehicle extending away from the street curb or roadway edge, and with the front of the vehicle away from the center of the street or roadway.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "42d4c802-c775-52b1-9d43-d1b3331884d9",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 570,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:2",
          "start": 451
        },
        "quote": "“Central business district” means that area bounded by Tyler Street, Madison Street, Second Street, and Huntoon Street.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "bbc4a13d-b864-5bf4-af8d-47a836725760",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 596,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:3",
          "start": 571
        },
        "quote": "“Parallel parking” means:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 4",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 4,
          "component_id": "cc39c2af-98b8-5b3e-9072-50add7b8bdb3",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 856,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:4",
          "start": 597
        },
        "quote": "(1) On streets with curbs, the standing or parking of the vehicle with the righthand wheels thereof parallel and within 12 inches of the righthand curb or roadway edge, subject to the exceptions permitting left side parallel parking as provided in this title.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:4#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 5",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 5,
          "component_id": "6615a35c-0c55-52f0-83bc-270a1ba0d379",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1112,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:5",
          "start": 857
        },
        "quote": "(2) On streets without curbs, the standing or parking of a motor vehicle with the righthand wheels thereof parallel with the right edge of the roadway so that at least 20 feet of the width of the roadway remains for the free movement of vehicular traffic.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:5#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 6",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 6,
          "component_id": "cc7d1c85-4c04-567b-9775-25c773743a28",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1262,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:6",
          "start": 1113
        },
        "quote": "“Street parking” means that portion of a street between the curb or lateral lines of a roadway and the adjacent lot lines not occupied by a sidewalk.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:6#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 7",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 7,
          "component_id": "ef526546-2f55-55d4-9591-e03836dea57d",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1448,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:7",
          "start": 1263
        },
        "quote": "“Traffic Division” means the Traffic Division of the City Police Department created by ordinance or such other unit of the Police Department as is designated functions under this title.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:7#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 8",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 8,
          "component_id": "ec08086a-7027-54b9-b950-baedb83e5912",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1662,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:8",
          "start": 1449
        },
        "quote": "“Traffic Engineer” means the Traffic Engineer of the City or any person designated by the Public Works Director or designee for the purpose of implementing and enforcing ordinances of the City relating to traffic.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:8#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 9",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 9,
          "component_id": "8ffd456c-c764-56cf-be90-bb60606eaf02",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1860,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:9",
          "start": 1663
        },
        "quote": "“Transportation Operations Division” means that division within the Public Works Department which has responsibility for street maintenance, traffic operations and on-street and off-street parking.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:9#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 10",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 10,
          "component_id": "b0bde471-b6dc-5870-94ad-8bacfeb41fe7",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1948,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:10",
          "start": 1861
        },
        "quote": "“Transportation Operations Superintendent” means the Public Works Director or designee.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:10#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 11",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 11,
          "component_id": "48cc77e0-f81d-55e4-a77f-9f34c8ac5b2e",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2292,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:11",
          "start": 1949
        },
        "quote": "“Vehicle” as used in TMC 10.25.010(b) means any vehicle propelled by power other than human power, designed to travel along the ground by use of wheels, tread, runners or slides, and transport persons or property or pull machinery and shall include, without limitation, automobiles, trucks, trailers, motorcycles, tractors, buggies and wagons.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:11#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 12",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 12,
          "component_id": "a9e8cc17-3c95-5e0d-84a0-7332d0cd27a9",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2299,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:12",
          "start": 2293
        },
        "quote": "Zones.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:12#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 13",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 13,
          "component_id": "6fa1ee78-3911-5c5e-8980-d60ca1f15d64",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2459,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:13",
          "start": 2300
        },
        "quote": "(1) “Curb loading zone” means a space adjacent to a curb reserved for the exclusive use of vehicles during the loading or unloading of passengers or materials.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:13#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 14",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 14,
          "component_id": "2ccf13d3-0da0-55fa-98c5-ba4329f840e3",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2660,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:14",
          "start": 2460
        },
        "quote": "(2) “No parking zones” means portions of streets designated by the Transportation Operations Superintendent as zones within which parking is prohibited at all times or at stated times when signposted.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:14#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 15",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 15,
          "component_id": "31734cd0-4c1e-5fb9-b899-d70c6021618e",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2875,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:15",
          "start": 2661
        },
        "quote": "(3) “No standing zones” means portions of streets designated by the Transportation Operations Superintendent as zones within which standing or stopping is prohibited at all times or at stated times when signposted.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:15#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 16",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 16,
          "component_id": "78a013d0-e7fc-50ce-b25e-5a174bd70572",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3032,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:16",
          "start": 2876
        },
        "quote": "(4) “Passenger curb loading zone” means a place adjacent to a curb reserved for the exclusive use of vehicles during the loading or unloading of passengers.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:16#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 17",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 17,
          "component_id": "6157123f-4be9-52a7-b7c9-6b3fa9380fbe",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3291,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:17",
          "start": 3033
        },
        "quote": "(5) “Safety zone” means the area of space officially set apart within a roadway for the exclusive use of pedestrians and which is protected or is so marked or indicated by adequate signs as to be plainly visible at all times while set apart as a safety zone.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:17#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 18",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 18,
          "component_id": "78b42a6a-2c74-5acc-9861-179839e0533b",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3536,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:18",
          "start": 3292
        },
        "quote": "(6) “Time-restricted parking zones” means portions of streets designated by the Transportation Operations Superintendent as zones within which the parking of vehicles is controlled and regulated by parking meters, pay stations or other methods.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:18#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 19",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 19,
          "component_id": "d93277ad-245a-5ed4-9fba-fe8b8eecaf15",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3702,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:19",
          "start": 3537
        },
        "quote": "Words and phrases not defined in this section shall have the meaning ascribed to them by the laws of the State relating to motor vehicles. (Ord. 20566 § 1, 6-10-25.)",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:19#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 20",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 20,
          "component_id": "c5cad990-3e42-5337-8503-2dfabeeffff0",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3758,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:20",
          "start": 3703
        },
        "quote": "Cross References: Definitions generally, TMC 1.10.020 .",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:20#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.05.010 block 21",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 21,
          "component_id": "c4172240-c665-57b9-8479-4eab310538fc",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 3841,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.010:block:21",
          "start": 3759
        },
        "quote": "State Law References: Definitions applicable to Traffic Act, K.S.A. 8-1401 et seq.",
